`Paper.Root` analyses the document and creates the `PaperState`. `Paper.Layer` turns in-text citations and "Fig. 3"-style references into links; the cards and lists read the model.

<Demo example="citations" height={580} />

## Anatomy

```svelte
<Paper.Root provider={defaultCitationProvider()}>
	<!-- inside each Viewer.Page -->
	<Paper.Layer />
	<Paper.Headings />
	<!-- anywhere inside -->
	<Paper.CitationCard />
	<Paper.CrossRefPreview />
	<Paper.References />
	<Paper.Figures />
</Paper.Root>
```

## Usage

- Click hooks (`onCitationClick`, `onCrossRefClick`, `onReferenceClick`) let your app open or import cited papers instead of jumping.
- `Paper.CitationCard layout="list"` shows every reference of a group like [1, 2, 3].
- `Paper.Headings` adds hidden real headings for screen readers and DOM-based tables of contents.

Guide: [Research papers](/docs/research-papers).

